          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "그래. 검에 남아 있던 그분의 힘으로 트롤을 몰아냈지. 봉인을 다 고칠 수는 없었지만, 사람들을 지킬 수는 있었단다."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.watch",
        "sourceId": "ch3.watch",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 5,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "함께 지킬 내일",
        "art": "together",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "스승님을 떠올리면 마음이 무거웠지. 그래도 내가 남은 건 이곳 사람들을 지키고 싶어서였단다. 그러다 보니 어느새 수십 년이 흘렀구나."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "이젠 혼자 안 해도 돼. 나도 있고 병사들도 있잖아. 우리 같이 지키자."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "그래, 함께 지키자꾸나. 너희가 있으니 나도 마음이 놓이는구나."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "en": {
    "title": "A Castle to Come Home To",
    "boy": "Pawn",
    "previewCount": 6,
    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "prologue",
        "sourceId": "prologue",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 0,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 5,
        "art": "prologue",
        "title": "Prologue",
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "Long ago, people built a castle over the seal that held the sleeping monsters. No one looked beneath it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "prologue.2",
        "sourceId": "prologue",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 0,
        "part": 2,
        "parts": 5,
        "art": "prologue_2",
        "title": "Prologue",
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "One night, the seal cracked. Monsters slipped out and battered the walls. Each tremor widened the breach."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "prologue.3",
        "sourceId": "prologue",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 0,
        "part": 3,
        "parts": 5,
        "art": "prologue_3",
        "title": "Prologue",
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The troll fled into the dark, a tooth broken. The old man’s sword had snapped too. At sunrise, the monsters retreated into the forest."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "prologue.4",
        "sourceId": "prologue",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 0,
        "part": 4,
        "parts": 5,
        "art": "prologue_4",
        "title": "Prologue",
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The defenders slept, exhausted. Only a boy too young to wield a spear was left to gather supplies."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "prologue.5",
        "sourceId": "prologue",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 0,
        "part": 5,
        "parts": 5,
        "art": "prologue_5",
        "title": "Prologue",
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The seal kept widening. The boy left the gate with an empty sack. Before sunset, he had to bring back enough for the castle to last another day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "supplies",
        "sourceId": "supplies",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 1,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "The Weight of an Empty Sack",
        "art": "supplies",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The boy’s timber braced the gate. After a warm meal, the soldiers returned to the walls."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "But all I did was bring back wood…"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Your wood kept the gate standing. You helped keep us safe."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Will you bring us more wood and food today?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Yes, I’ll try!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ring",
        "sourceId": "ring",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 2,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "You Need Not Stand Alone",
        "art": "ring",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "If I make the ring, could I fight like you?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes. You can draw on a hero’s power to fight, just as I did."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Can I talk to the hero in the ring, too?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes. The voice in my sword helped me, too. But how you fight is for you to decide."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "And don’t try to hold them all off alone. When my sword broke, the people in the castle stood together."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "troll",
        "sourceId": "troll",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 3,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "After the Sword Broke",
        "art": "troll",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The morning after the broken-toothed troll fell, the old man quietly ran his hand over the gate."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "We held them off, even without your sword."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes. Now we can defend the castle together, even without my sword."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "spring",
        "sourceId": "spring",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 4,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "Against the Tide",
        "art": "spring",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Monster tracks. Where do you think this path leads?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "I’ve never come this far either. I always fought them at the castle gate."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Then let’s go together. Maybe we can block the way they use to reach us."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "summer",
        "sourceId": "summer",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 5,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "Paths in the Stone",
        "art": "summer",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "Beyond spring stood an old waystone. Its carved paths branched outward from a single castle."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "All these paths lead to our castle. I was so focused on the seal beneath it that I never knew."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Then let’s check them one by one. There must be a path we can close."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "autumn",
        "sourceId": "autumn",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 6,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "What Must Not Be Passed On",
        "art": "autumn",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The same mark lay beneath fallen leaves. The old man thought of his years on the walls."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "I can really count on you now. Still, I hope you won’t spend your whole life guarding the walls as I did."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Then you have to rest too. Let’s make sure we both can when we get home."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "winter",
        "sourceId": "winter",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 7,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "From the Other Side",
        "art": "winter",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "The spirit lit up the snow-covered waystone. Carved into it was a way to close the path leading home."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "If we close this path, the monsters will have to turn back too. Let’s seal it once we’re safely across."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Yes. Then the people at the castle can rest a little too, right?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "home",
        "sourceId": "home",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 8,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 2,
        "title": "Today, You Can Rest",
        "art": "route_seal",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "After they returned, the wisps’ light sealed one path. For once, a quiet morning came to the castle gates."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "home.part2",
        "sourceId": "home",
        "chapter": 1,
        "scene": 8,
        "part": 2,
        "parts": 2,
        "title": "Today, You Can Rest",
        "art": "home",
        "lineStart": 1,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "What should I bring back today?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Today, you can rest."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 0,
            "text": "Other paths still remained. Before night came again, they sat together and shared a loaf of bread."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch2.return",
        "sourceId": "ch2.return",
        "chapter": 2,
        "scene": 1,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "Beneath the Seal",
        "art": "records",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "We closed a path, but I still hear something underground. Did the seal break again?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "We can’t tell yet. We closed one path, but we haven’t fully repaired the seal beneath the castle."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "How did they make the seal in the first place? Let’s look for records in the castle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch2.rift",
        "sourceId": "ch2.rift",
        "chapter": 2,
        "scene": 2,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "When the Earth Split",
        "art": "first_rift",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "The old records tell of people living alongside spirits. Then one day, the earth shook."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Why? Did someone split the earth open?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "The records do not say why. Monsters poured out of the cracks, and the soldiers grew weary of endless fighting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch2.heroes",
        "sourceId": "ch2.heroes",
        "chapter": 2,
        "scene": 3,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 2,
        "title": "A Power Shared",
        "art": "spirit_gift",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "The Spirit King shared his power with the kingdom’s defenders. As it took hold, their bodies grew smaller and their faces younger."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch2.heroes.part2",
        "sourceId": "ch2.heroes",
        "chapter": 2,
        "scene": 3,
        "part": 2,
        "parts": 2,
        "title": "A Power Shared",
        "art": "heroes_battle",
        "lineStart": 1,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Were all the people who received that power knights?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "No. There were knights with shields, and mages too. They became the heroes of the old stories."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch2.castle",
        "sourceId": "ch2.castle",
        "chapter": 2,
        "scene": 4,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "What Lies Beneath",
        "art": "heroes_seal",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "The heroes drove the monsters back and sealed the rift together. The kingdom built this castle to guard the seal."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "So when we repair the gate, we’re protecting the seal too."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "That’s right. With the soldiers holding the walls and you bringing supplies, we can keep the seal safe too."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch2.seal",
        "sourceId": "ch2.seal",
        "chapter": 2,
        "scene": 5,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "The Wound Remains",
        "art": "seal_watch",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "So it took several heroes working together. Closing one path isn’t the end for us either."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "But closing that path gave everyone a chance to breathe. We’ll find a way to deal with the rest together."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "I’ll help defend it tonight, too. Now I know why this castle stands here."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.master",
        "sourceId": "ch3.master",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 1,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "A Name Remembered",
        "art": "mars_master",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Now I’ll tell you about the day the seal was broken again. It concerns my old master, the knight Mars."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "The strongest knight in the kingdom? He was your teacher?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes. He taught me to hold a sword, and to get back up after a fall. I looked up to him."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.glory",
        "sourceId": "ch3.glory",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 2,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "The Knight Who Sought Glory",
        "art": "heroes_valor",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "My master often spoke of the old heroes. He said he was waiting for his chance to save the kingdom."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "But isn’t it good when there’s no need to fight?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "I think so too. But my master said that without a battle, no one would see the skill he’d spent his life building."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.breach",
        "sourceId": "ch3.breach",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 3,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 2,
        "title": "The Second Fracture",
        "art": "mars_breaks_seal",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "One night, I followed him below the castle. As he drove his sword into the seal, he said he would slay the monsters that came out and become a hero."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "He let the monsters out on purpose… just to become a hero?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.breach.part2",
        "sourceId": "ch3.breach",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 3,
        "part": 2,
        "parts": 2,
        "title": "The Second Fracture",
        "art": "mars_breach",
        "lineStart": 2,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes. But even he couldn’t stop the ancient troll. While I was leading people to safety, I lost sight of him behind the falling stones."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.sword",
        "sourceId": "ch3.sword",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 4,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "When the Sword Answered",
        "art": "young_guardian",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "The monsters returned every night. When I picked up an old sword in the armoury, I heard a voice."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "Was that the Guardian’s voice? Did he help you?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes. With his power still in the sword, I drove the troll back. I couldn’t fully mend the seal, but I could protect the people."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch3.watch",
        "sourceId": "ch3.watch",
        "chapter": 3,
        "scene": 5,
        "part": 1,
        "parts": 1,
        "title": "Tomorrow, Together",
        "art": "together",
        "lineStart": 0,
        "lines": [
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Thinking of my master weighed on me. But I stayed because I wanted to protect the people here. Before I knew it, decades had passed."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 1,
            "text": "You don’t have to do it alone anymore. I’m here, and so are the soldiers. Let’s defend it together."
          },
          {
            "speaker": 2,
            "text": "Yes, together. Knowing you’re all here puts my mind at ease."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "ja": {
